<topic id="GUID-F5C640A6-6B4A-4A14-93AA-3FB3C0EF86FE" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>ThETA Ibatt-rms Control</title> 
  <body> 
    <p> ThETA Ibatt-rms feature (sometimes referred to as ThETA or Ibatt) is intended to control battery current in order to protect and control battery reliability. This is an optional feature that is disabled by default.
    </p> 
    <p> When activated, it allows OEM/ODM to use a control mechanism for battery current. Currently, OEMS can achieve similar effect by reducing PL4/PL2/PL1 in DC mode but at higher performance penalty.
    </p> 
    <p> BIOS shall add control feature for Ibatt-rms where the following register values below (ISYS_CONTROL) need to be set by OEM/ODM
    </p> 
    <table id="TABLE_AFCC64746804464E8777A2896A5A009F">
      <tgroup cols="4"><colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="*" /><colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="*" /><colspec colnum="3" colname="col3" colwidth="*" /><colspec colname="col4" colnum="4" colwidth="1.33*" /><thead>
          <row>
            <entry colname="col1">Knob
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col2">Description
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col3">Ownership
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col4">Interface
            </entry>
          </row></thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry colname="col1">Isys_L1
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col2">The sustained current level, higher currents are allowed but will be clipped in 10's of seconds
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col3">OEM/ODM configurable by BIOS
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col4">ISYS_CONTROL_0_0_0_MCHBAR_ISYS_CURRENT_LIMIT_L1
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry colname="col1">Isys_L2
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col2">Peak current level, higher currents are possible but will be clipped in 10's msec range
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col3">OEM/ODM configurable by BIOS
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col4">ISYS_CONTROL_0_0_0_MCHBAR_ISYS_CURRENT_LIMIT_L2
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry colname="col1">tau_L1
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col2">L1 tau for EMWA calculation, expected to be 10's of sec
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col3">OEM/ODM configurable by BIOS
            </entry>
            <entry colname="col4">ISYS_CONTROL_0_0_0_MCHBAR_ISYS_CURRENT_L1_TAU
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </table>
  </body> 
